# file(1) magic for the Bovnar (BVNR) typed, unit-aware serialisation format.
#
# The *.bvnr extension is the AUTHORITATIVE signal (see the shared-mime-info
# glob); this content magic is a best-effort fallback for extension-less files.
# It matches a top-level assignment line — ".<identifier> = ..." at column 0,
# i.e. preceded by a newline — within the first 256 lines, skipping leading
# "#" comments and blank lines.
#
# Heuristic limitations (acceptable because the extension is authoritative):
#   * A document whose very first byte begins the assignment (no comment/blank
#     header line) is identified by extension only.
#   * A non-Bovnar text file that embeds a Bovnar document at column 0 (e.g. a
#     Markdown README with a ```bovnar code block) may match.
# The newline anchor deliberately avoids false positives on source code such as
# "self.port = 8080" or "module.exports = ...", where the dotted name is not at
# the start of a line.
#
# Compile and use:
#     file -C -m bovnar.magic            # produces bovnar.magic.mgc
#     file -m bovnar.magic FILE          # human-readable type
#     file --mime-type -m bovnar.magic FILE
#
# Install so plain `file` uses it (Linux):
#     cat bovnar.magic >> /etc/magic && (cd /etc && file -C)   # or
#     install -Dm644 bovnar.magic ~/.magic && file -C -m ~/.magic
#
0	regex/256l	\n\\.[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*[[:blank:]]*=	Bovnar document
!:mime	text/vnd.bovnar
!:ext	bvnr
